# Snowman portfolio

This repository contains a personal portfolio website built with plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript. It is designed to run from the repository root on GitHub Pages and is editable in-page using a lightweight local editor.

## How to enable GitHub Pages
1. Open the repository in GitHub.
2. Go to Settings -> Pages.
3. Set the source to the main branch and the root folder `/`.
4. Save the settings and wait a minute or two for the first deploy.

## How to enter edit mode
- Open the site in a browser and append `#edit` to the URL, for example `https://username.github.io/repo/#edit`.
- You can also press `Ctrl + Shift + E` anywhere on the site.
- In edit mode, the toolbar appears and each editable field can be changed in place.

## How to create a personal access token
1. Go to GitHub -> Settings -> Developer settings -> Personal access tokens.
2. Create a fine-grained token for this repository only.
3. Grant it Contents: `Read and write` access.
4. Paste the token into the browser prompt when you click Publish.
5. The token is stored in `sessionStorage` only and is not saved in the repository.

## How to publish
1. Enter edit mode.
2. Click Publish from the toolbar.
3. If the token has not been entered yet, the app will prompt for it.
4. The app will detect the repository automatically from the Pages URL when possible, or you can override it using the Repo button in the toolbar.
5. The file is updated through the GitHub REST API using the existing `content.json` SHA.
6. After publishing, note that GitHub Pages can take about a minute to redeploy.

## How to export and import
- Click Export to download the current `content.json` file.
- Click Import to load a previous or edited `content.json` file.
- The imported file is validated before being applied.

## Assumptions made
- The site is intended to live on a GitHub Pages URL of the form `username.github.io/repo` or `username.github.io`.
- If the repository cannot be inferred from the URL, the app prompts for `owner/repo` and stores the override in localStorage.
- Placeholder content is used so the portfolio looks complete on first load.
- Uploaded profile/project images are converted to compressed JPEG data URLs with a max width of 1200px and quality of 0.8.
- Drafts are stored in localStorage under `snowman_portfolio_draft` for autosave, while the GitHub token is stored only in `sessionStorage` under `snowman_portfolio_token`.
- The editor assumes no external libraries and keeps the final site compatible with a static GitHub Pages deployment.

## Files
- `index.html` — page structure and editor toolbar
- `styles.css` — modern responsive styling and theme variables
- `app.js` — data loading, rendering, editor logic, autosave, export/import, and publish flow
- `content.json` — the primary editable site content
- `.nojekyll` — ensures static file hosting works correctly on GitHub Pages

## Notes
- All rendered user content is rendered through text nodes or `textContent` to reduce XSS risk.
- The design supports light and dark mode automatically via `prefers-color-scheme`, and there is a manual toggle in the site header as well as a default scheme in the editor toolbar.
- The repository is designed to work from the main branch root, as requested.
